@@@@ EDIT docs/configuration.md
@@@@ FIND
The breaker counts requests, not attempts.

## [rate_limit]

@@@@ REPLACE
The breaker counts requests, not attempts.

## [retry]

| key | default | meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `max_attempts` | `3` | attempts allowed for one request, the first included (1 to 10) |
| `base_delay` | `100ms` | wait after the first failed attempt |
| `factor` | `2` | multiplier applied to the wait after each further failure (1 to 10) |
| `max_delay` | `5s` | longest a computed backoff may grow to; must not be shorter than `base_delay` |
| `honor_retry_after` | `true` | let a server `Retry-After` lengthen the wait |

Only failures that can succeed on a second try are retried: timeouts, resets, refused connections
and the statuses 408, 429, 500, 502, 503 and 504. Every other failure ends the request at once.
`max_delay` bounds the computed backoff only; a `Retry-After` is bounded by `max_wait` and the
request `deadline`. Invalid values are rejected when the configuration loads.

## [rate_limit]

@@@@ END
